.el .ds Aq '
.TH ziv 1  "ziv 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
ziv \- OME\-Zarr IIIF tile server + static exporter
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBziv\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
ziv is a single, zero\-install binary that turns an OME\-Zarr image into IIIF Image API 3.0 tiles — either as a live HTTP server (`ziv serve`) or a self\-contained static tile tree (`ziv export`) you can drop on any static host. Both commands accept a local filesystem path or a remote store URL (s3://, gs://, az://, http(s)://).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ziv\-serve(1)
Serve one or more OME\-Zarr images as a live IIIF Image API 3.0 server
.TP
ziv\-export(1)
Export an OME\-Zarr image as a self\-contained static IIIF Image API 3.0 Level\-0 tile tree: every tile file OpenSeadragon v3 will request, a level0 info.json that pins the finite request space, and an embedded viewer. Drop the output directory on any static host (S3/GitHub Pages/CDN) for a live zoomable image with zero backend
.TP
ziv\-render(1)
Render one projection of an OME\-Zarr image to a single PNG or JPEG file
.TP
ziv\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
